# log.md2 — Development Log (Session 2)

## 2026-03-06 — Cursed Portrait Glow Frame + Tooltip; Shadowfingers Modal Restyle

### What
1. **Cursed player portrait frame**: when a player has active curses, the CharacterPortrait border turns purple (`border-purple-500`) with an outer glowing box-shadow. A Radix Tooltip shows on hover listing each curse's name (via `getHexById`) and weeks remaining.
2. **SideInfoTabs outer wrapper**: the outer gold frame also switches to purple + glow, since `overflow-hidden` would otherwise clip CharacterPortrait's own glow effect.
3. **All call sites updated**: `SideInfoTabs`, `PlayerInfoPanel`, `MobileHUD`, `SpectatorPanel`, `SpectatorOverlay`, `TurnOrderPanel`, `ResourcePanel`, `PlayersTab`, `AnimatedPlayerToken`, `PlayerToken` — all now pass `curses={player.activeCurses}`.
4. **ShadowfingersModal restyle**: replaced `DialogDescription` (low-contrast italic) with `font-display text-card-foreground` text. Newspaper headline uses parchment/scroll background matching the rest of the game. `gold-button` for Continue. Stolen items list also styled consistently.

### Why
- User reported portrait frame had no visual curse feedback visible from outside the component; overflow-hidden clipped the inner glow
- Shadowfingers text was hard to read (low contrast `text-muted-foreground italic`)

### Files
- `src/components/game/CharacterPortrait.tsx` — curses prop, CurseTooltipWrapper, purple border + glow
- `src/components/game/ShadowfingersModal.tsx` — EventPanel-style restyle
- 10 other call sites — curses/hasCurse props propagated

